  "body": "Found by the release QA swarm (#2582) on **v0.24.0**, driven through `camcraft-cli mcp` by a Codex agent.\n\n## What happens\nStart from a project with an implicit setup and eight operations in machining order: Face, Pocket, Outside, Spot5, DrillThrough, TapDrill, TapCycle, Chamfer. Then `add_setup {name:\"PlateSetup\"}` and `set_operation_setup {operation:<op>, setup:\"PlateSetup\"}` once per operation, **in that order**. `get_job` then shows:\n\nChamfer, DrillThrough, Face, Outside, Pocket, Spot5, TapCycle, TapDrill\n\ni.e. alphabetical. The tap now comes before its tap drill and drilling before facing. Generation does stop the unsafe one (`DrillThrough: invalid machining parameters: R plane Z 12.000 is below the stock top Z 13.000 ...`), but the tap-before-pilot order is not caught by that check.\n\n## Expected\nMoving operations into a setup keeps their relative order (or appends each in the order moved). The program order is the user's.\n\n## Reproduce\nOn skull: `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/q01-offset-test.camproj` (correct order) -> the calls above; result saved as `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/q01-setup-order.camproj`. Calls: `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/evidence.jsonl` steps 107-118; `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/REPORT.md` (P7). Workaround: `reorder_operation` every op back.\n\nNot checked on current main.\n\nDone means: moving operations into a named setup keeps their program order, pinned by a test (command + MCP).\n",
